CloudBurrow patch 2 of 5 to github.com/goccy/googlesqlite v0.3.1
(cloudburrow/cloudburrow#1061; the bug: #1043, #1047).

The bug: Catalog.tvfHandleForSpec (internal/catalog.go, line 2651 in v0.3.1)
returns tvf.TableValuedFunction, the handle embedded in the
*FixedOutputSchemaTVF that go-googlesql's NewFixedOutputSchemaTVF returned,
and the SimpleCatalog keeps only that inner handle. go-googlesql puts the
finalizer that deletes the C++ object on the outer handle, which nothing then
references, so the next garbage collection freed a table function the catalog
still pointed at; its next use crashed the process (SIGSEGV in the
WebAssembly engine) and every dataset was lost. The fix keeps each outer
handle referenced for the life of the Catalog. tvf_gc_test.go crashes without
the fix and passes with it.

